      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T22:53:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m worried that `--native` re-execs forever on a kernel whose native page size isn\u0027t 16KB (4KB arm64 or x86_64). `exec_native()` succeeds there, and `sysconf(_SC_PAGESIZE)` still returns 4KB in the new image, so it takes this branch again. Nothing runs `--native` today, so this only happens when someone runs it by hand.\n\nWould it be OK to drop the `--native` mode and use `P3S_COMPAT_MAIN(run_test)`? If you\u0027d like to keep it, could it re-exec only from a 4KB process (`p3s_is_compat_process()`) and skip when the page size still isn\u0027t `NATIVE_PAGE_SIZE`? `vmalloc_align_p3s.c` and a few other tests later in the chain have the same `main()`.",
